{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>פנה</b> — He stated that the building of Zion will come about because of Israel's prayer in exile, they being like a broom tree in the desert. And the one who says that Israel is called ערער on account of ערו ערו — this is not correct, for those who say ערו ערו are the Edomites, the Babylonians, as I will explain in its place."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {0 "The phrase ערו ערו (\"strip, strip bare\") likely alludes to Psalm 137:7 or a similar passage; resolved as Edomites/Babylonians based on the standard identification in medieval exegetical tradition."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:51.478199102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}